            <ArticleTitle>Iron(II)-Catalyzed Direct Synthesis of NH Sulfoximines from Sulfoxides.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>324-327</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/anie.201710498</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Free NH-sulfoximines were directly prepared from sulfoxides through iron catalysis by applying a readily available, shelf-stable hydroxylamine triflic acid salt. No additional oxidant is needed, and the substrate scope is broad, including a range of heterocyclic compounds.</AbstractText>
